<title>NORWAY: Aker RGI shares up 5 pct on Scancem offer.</title>
<headline>Aker RGI shares up 5 pct on Scancem offer.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Norwegian industrial holding group Aker RGI ASA jumped more than five percent on Tuesday after the company said it had been approached to sell its stake in Nordic cement group Scancem.</p>
<p>Aker RGI and Swedish Skanska AB each own 33.3 percent of Scancem.</p>
<p>Aker said several parties had contacted it over a possible sale but that it had no plans to sell up.</p>
<p>A source close to Aker RGI said the company had been offered &quot;significantly higher&quot; than 300 Swedish crowns per share in Scancem. Aker declined to confirm that level.</p>
<p>At 1139 GMT Aker RGI's A share was up 9.50 crowns at 180 crowns in light turnover of 14.5 million crowns.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
